      "claim_id": "sql_rawdb/Q1.3/001",
      "line": 20,
      "text": "Based on the database search, several measured density values have been reported for an equimolar (mole fraction = 0.5) propan-2-ol + water liquid mixture at 25 °C (298.15 K) and atmospheric pressure (~101 kPa). However, careful verification of the source blocks reveals that many initial matches were actually different chemical systems (ternary mixtures, different alcohols, or different composition bases such as molality or mass fraction).",
